{"reference":"Song of Songs 3","book":"Song of Songs","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A repeated charge about love","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verse 5 repeats a refrain addressed to the daughters of Jerusalem about not stirring or awakening love until it pleases. It marks a concern with love’s arousal or timing, but the wording’s precise force is disputed and does not establish a universal modern timetable for relationships.","verse_refs":["Song of Songs 3:5"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_song_of_songs_003_1b49863a51743687034b2314"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading the Song’s shifting scenes","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The Song as a whole uses recurring refrains, searches, descriptions, and vivid images to create poetic coherence. Its sequence, however, does not establish one uncontested continuous drama, wedding cycle, dream plot, or biography. That caution is useful in this chapter, where the night search and the splendid procession are placed beside one another without requiring a single agreed account of how every scene fits a plot.","verse_refs":["Song of Songs 1:2-17","Song of Songs 2:1-17","Song of Songs 4:1-16","Song of Songs 5:1-16","Song of Songs 6:1-13","Song of Songs 7:1-13","Song of Songs 8:1-14"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_song_of_songs_003_6356294eff2314f6738229d1"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Ancient Egyptian and Mesopotamian love poetry provides substantial parallels to the Song’s multiple voices, imagery, fragrance, body praise, and landscapes. Such parallels help readers recognize the Song’s poetic love language without proving that it derives from one source or from a cult ritual. Later Jewish and Christian traditions have also read the Song allegorically, but its speakers do not explicitly identify themselves in those terms.","verse_refs":["Song of Songs 1","Song of Songs 1:1-17","Song of Songs 1:2-17","Song of Songs 2:1-17","Song of Songs 4:1-16","Song of Songs 5:1-16","Song of Songs 6:1-13","Song of Songs 7:1-13","Song of Songs 8:1-14"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_song_of_songs_003_7eb68042174e79a81bb82d12"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}